                  5. Common Real-Time Errors
ImagePullBackOff: Image unavailable, private registry, or wrong access permissions. 12
CrashLoopBackOff: Liveness/readiness probe timeout is too short for the application to start (e.g., app needs 300 seconds but probe is set to 5 seconds). 34
Pod Not Starting: Insufficient CPU/memory on the cluster node — always check node size. 56
Service Not Accessible: Wrong port mapping (e.g., configured 8099 instead of 8080) or network policy blocking traffic. 7
Node Not Ready: Invalid certificate, network issue, hardware failure, or cloud region out of capacity. 8910
Debug command: kubectl describe node <node-name> → check the Events section for clues. 1112
6. Taints & Tolerations
Use case: When patching a specific node (e.g., Node 2 out of 3), first drain all pods to other nodes, block new pods from scheduling on it (taint), perform patching, then re-enable. 131415
Taint = blocks new pods; Toleration = allows exceptions to that block. 1617
